title: 'cumulus: compute resubmittable segment in the parent search'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |
    The slot-based collator's parent search now also returns the V3 resubmittable segment: the
    parachain blocks above the relay-known head (pending availability if any, else included) up to
    the best parent, oldest first. It is reconstructed by walking the chosen parent's ancestry, and
    is empty for V2 and for a V3 search that finds nothing to resubmit. `ParentSearchResult` gains
    `resubmittable_segment` and a `v3_enabled` flag, plus `walk_best_parent_back` and
    `fall_back_to_included` that keep the segment in sync as the search walks the best parent back.
    Nothing consumes the segment yet; the resubmission work that follows does.
crates:
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-common
  bump: minor
- name: cumulus-client-consensus-aura
  bump: patch
